title: The Independents at Leipzig
subtitle: The USPD moves to the left.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 12 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: repression -= 5

= The Independents at Leipzig

From 30 November to 6 December the Independent Social Democrats held their congress in Leipzig. The party has grown to three-quarters of a million members, many times our own, and its left wing won. The congress adopted an action programme for the dictatorship of the proletariat on the basis of the councils, left the Second International and resolved to negotiate with the Communist International.

Their right wing, Hilferding and Kautsky's friends, still sit in the leadership. Their left, Däumig, Stoecker and Koenen of Halle, talk of joining Moscow. [? if kapd_split = 1 : Our own party is half the size it was in October. ?][? if heidelberg_outcome = 3 : Our Left Radical Zentrale despises the Independents as parliamentarians. ?] Karl Radek, about to be released from Moabit and sent home, writes that the future of German communism is in the USPD's left wing.

- @letter: Propose joint action to the whole USPD.
- @left_wing: Win the USPD's left wing for the International.
- @denounce: Denounce the Independent leaders as centrists.
- @alone: No dealings with any parliamentary party.

@letter
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's answer: unity in action, now.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
