The Zentrale's open letter proposes joint campaigns for the councils and against the state of siege. The USPD's leaders reply politely. Its members, in many towns, reply by turning up.

@left_wing
subtitle: The Spartacist strategy: bring the Independents' best workers to communism, and the party will be a mass party.
on-arrival: leipzig_line = 2; uspd_relation += 6; world_revolution += 3; independence -= 2; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6; lean_luxemburgist += 2

Our people seek out Koenen in Halle and Stoecker in Berlin. The talk is of a single Communist party, with the Independents' masses and our principles. It will take a year.

@denounce
subtitle: The Left's answer: the Independents must be broken, not courted.
on-arrival: leipzig_line = 3; uspd_relation -= 10; militancy += 3; offensive_satisfaction += 6; lean_offensive += 2

Our paper calls the Leipzig programme a fig leaf for Kautsky and Hilferding. The Independent workers who read it are not grateful.

@alone
subtitle: The Left Radicals' line: the councils, and nothing else.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: leipzig_line = 4; uspd_relation -= 6; ultraleft_satisfaction += 6; lean_ultraleft += 2

The party ignores the Independents' congress as it ignored the National Assembly. The Independents do not ignore us: they are recruiting in our districts.
